//! Coarse LOD levels: Chunks above level 0, derived and never edited.
//!
//! A level-k Chunk is the [`downsample`] of eight level-(k-1) Chunks, generated by the
//! level-(k-1) source generator because the Server holds level 0 only within `evict` of
//! the Eye. From [`COLUMNS_FROM`] up, a Chunk nothing changed is generated at its own
//! Voxel size instead, one height per column and no caves. Level 1 takes the level-0 Chunks the [`ChunkStore`] holds instead, so an Edit
//! reaches it, and reads a changed one with its fluid and fire ([`downsample_changed`]).
//! Nothing here simulates: level 1 is a picture of what level 0 holds, and levels above
//! it show what the generator made.
//!
//! [`downsample`]: tesserae_core::downsample
//!
//! Meshed by the level-0 mesher. No light is stored above level 0: a face is lit open sky unless it
//! looks into air under the terrain, which the mesh job works out from the generator.
//! The job pipeline is ADR-0007's: `docs/adr/0007-streaming-jobs-run-on-bevy-task-pools.md`.

